    "content": "Generation Z, often called \"Zoomers,\" includes people born between 1997 and 2012. As of 2026, this generation is approximately 14 to 29 years old. Following Millennials, this cohort is defined by being \"digital natives\" who grew up with smartphones and social media, with many experiencing increased awareness of mental health and social issues. Key Details About Gen Z: Birth Years: 1997 – 2012 Age Range (2026): 14 – 29 Nickname: iGeneration, Zoomers, Post-Millennials Defining Characteristics: High digital literacy, high ethnic/racial diversity, and a pragmatic, often socially conscious outlook. Contextual Boundaries: End of Millennials: 1996 Start of Gen Alpha: 2013 While some analysts may vary the years by one or two, 1997-2012 is the most widely accepted definition.",
